com/images/courses/coding-patterns/sliding-windows/introduction-to-sliding-=
windows/image-05-00-3-3VYLULRX.svg?dpl=3Ddpl_CEjisbLnWxFQGUTRjiHGoKY1oV5c">=
</div></figure>
</li>
<li>
<p>To <strong>slide</strong> the window is to advance both the left and rig=
ht pointers:</p>
<figure class=3D"py-1"><div style=3D"display:flex;justify-content:center"><=
img alt=3D"Image represents a visual depiction of a 'slide' operation in a =
data structure, likely an array or list.  The left side shows an initial st=
ate with a light-blue, rounded-rectangle representing the data structure co=
ntaining several black dots representing elements.  Above this structure ar=
e two gray rectangular boxes labeled 'left' and 'right,' indicating the sou=
rce of data insertion.  Solid arrows point downwards from 'left' and 'right=
' to the leftmost and rightmost elements of the data structure, respectivel=
y.  A horizontal arrow labeled 'slide' points to the right, separating the =
before and after states. The right side shows the data structure after the =
